The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. Women's rights;
b. obligations and responsibilities of the Regency Regional Government; c. women's empowerment;
d. women's protection;
e. strategy for women's empowerment and protection;
f. implementation of women's protection;
g. mechanism for organizing women's empowerment and protection; h. financing; and
i. guidance and supervision.

Article 9
Empowerment of women in the social and cultural field as referred to in Article 7 letter b shall be implemented through:
a. enhancement of knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of tiered education in accordance with potential to improve social status;
b. enhancement of awareness, willingness and ability to overcome;
c. health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts primarily in the field of reproductive health;
d. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about family planning;
e. independence, health and welfare including access to consultation services and marriage registration; and
f. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

